===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*sehs}}, whence also {{cog|ofs|sex}}, {{cog|osx|sehs}}, {{cog|dum|sesse}} ({{cog|nl|zes}}), {{cog|goh|sehs}} ({{cog|de|sechs}}), {{cog|non|sex}} ({{cog|sv|sex}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐌰𐌹𐌷𐍃}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*swéḱs}}, cognate with {{cog|grc|ἕξ}}, {{cog|la|sex}}, {{cog|sga|se|sē}} ({{cog|ga|sé}}), {{cog|sla-pro|*šestь}} ({{cog|ru|шесть}}).

